## Usage

Run `{{project_slug}}` in a terminal for the full-screen UI. Press `?` for its keys and `q` to quit.

<!-- stacks:fill What a person does in the UI, in two or three lines. -->

Without a terminal (a pipe, a script, CI) it prints instead and exits:

```bash
{{project_slug}} --no-tui          # an aligned text table
{{project_slug}} --json | jq .     # {"tasks": [...]}
{{project_slug}} --tasks tasks.json
```

See [docs/configuration.md](docs/configuration.md) for flags, environment variables and exit statuses.

## Development

Requires rustup (the toolchain comes from `rust-toolchain.toml`) and make.

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `make build` | Release binary in `target/release/` |
| `make test` | Unit, frame snapshot, event loop and binary tests |
| `make snapshots` | Rewrite frame snapshots after a deliberate view change |
| `make lint` | rustfmt check and clippy with warnings denied |
| `make audit` | cargo-deny: advisories, licenses, sources |
| `make ci` | Everything CI runs |

See [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) for how the code is laid out.

